Data sources (web → native P1/S8 seam, NO view HTTP):
  useVehicles + useQuery(`/drives?vehicle_id=…&limit=5`) + useUnits + useDateFormat + useTranslation
  → RecentDrivesSource pushes a coalesced RecentDrivesUpdate {status, connection, isFetching, drives,
    units, updatedAt}; the model projects it; the view only switches over phase + renders rows.

Parity arithmetic reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform value parity, NOT a
"corrected" version):
  distance = convertDistanceFromSI(distance_m ?? 0, unitPrefs.distance)
           = metres / { 1000 km · 1609.344 mi · 0.3048 ft } ; rendered fmtNumber(_, 1) + unit
  minutes  = fmtInt((duration_s ?? 0) / 60)                  [fmtNumber(_, 0)]
  soc      = start_soc_pct ?? '?'  /  end_soc_pct ?? '?'     [raw JS number stringification]
  date     = formatDateShort(start_ts) = toLocaleDateString(locale,{month:'short',day:'numeric'})
             via "MMMd" template, or '—' for missing/invalid
  detail   = `${minutes} min · ${start}% → ${end}%`          [single localizable positional format]
  rows     = last 5 (registry "recent-drives")
  fmtNumber = locale-grouped, fixed fraction digits, half-away-from-zero (Intl.NumberFormat default).

